{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"173","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Rock-Paper-Scissors"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nikephoros and Polycarpus play rock-paper-scissors. The loser gets pinched (not too severely!)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us remind you the rules of this game. Rock-paper-scissors is played by two players. In each round the players choose one of three items independently from each other. They show the items with their hands: a rock, scissors or paper. The winner is determined by the following rules: the rock beats the scissors, the scissors beat the paper and the paper beats the rock. If the players choose the same item, the round finishes with a draw."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nikephoros and Polycarpus have played "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" rounds. In each round the winner gave the loser a friendly pinch and the loser ended up with a fresh and new red spot on his body. If the round finished in a draw, the players did nothing and just played on."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nikephoros turned out to have worked out the following strategy: before the game began, he chose some sequence of items "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A = (a1, a2, ..., am)"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then he cyclically showed the items from this sequence, starting from the first one. Cyclically means that Nikephoros shows signs in the following order: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"..."},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"am"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"..."},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"am"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"..."},{"kind":"text","text":" and so on. Polycarpus had a similar strategy, only he had his own sequence of items "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"B = (b1, b2, ..., bk)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the number of red spots on both players after they've played "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" rounds of the game. You can consider that when the game began, the boys had no red spots on them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 2·109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of the game's rounds."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a string of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters and the third line contains sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"B"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a string of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m, k ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The given lines only contain characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Character \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" stands for the rock, character \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" represents the scissors and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" represents the paper."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print two space-separated integers: the numbers of red spots Nikephoros and Polycarpus have."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\nRPS\nRSPP\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\nRRRRRRRR\nR\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the game went like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R - R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Draw. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P - S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Nikephoros loses. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S - P"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Polycarpus loses. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R - P"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Nikephoros loses. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P - R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Polycarpus loses. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S - S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Draw. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R - P"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Nikephoros loses. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, in total Nikephoros has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" losses (and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" red spots), and Polycarpus only has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"173A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/173/problem/A"}